From 8b548e24cd2874517f8bee27531b844648897294 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:15:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] perf(render): reset only dirty occlusion cache blocks

The occlusion worker reset its whole ArrayOcclusionCache (13.5 MiB at render
distance 12, 256 MiB from 32) with Arrays.fill on every cycle. Use a cache
with the same byte layout, index arithmetic and exceptions that marks each
64-byte block becoming non-zero, and zero only marked blocks on reset.

Also return false directly for boxes whose every cell lies outside the cache
cube, after the camera-inside check. The library already skips each such cell
because its cache lookup returns -1 and then returns false without casting a
ray or touching the cache. Unsorted, oversized or near-overflow boxes still go
through the library.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
